<title>SWEDEN: Nordbanken in $250 mln Iran financing deal.</title>
<headline>Nordbanken in $250 mln Iran financing deal.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish bank Nordbanken said on Thursday it had signed an agreement to finance Swedish exports to Iran.</p>
<p>&quot;The deals total $250 million and has been signed with Iran's five leading commercial banks, in consultation with the central bank Bank Markazi,&quot; Nordbanken said in a statement.  </p>
<p>The deals are conditional on guarantees from the Swedish export credit authority (EKN), the bank said.</p>
<p>Iranian banks have signed similar deals with leading German, Belgian, Swiss, Austrian and Spanish banks with guarantees from those countries' export credit institutions, Nordbanken said.</p>
<p>&quot;The deal meets a large demand within Swedish export industry and increases Swedish competitiveness on the expanding Iranian market,&quot; the bank said.</p>
<p>-- Birgitta Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
